===Etymology 1===
From {{inh|en|enm|rys}}, from {{der|en|fro|ris}}, from {{der|en|roa-oit|riso}}, {{m|it|risi}}, from {{der|en|gkm|ὄρυζα}}, from an Eastern {{der|en|ira|-}} language related to {{cog|pal|blnj|tr=*brinǰ}}, {{cog|kmr|riz}} (beyond euphrates) and {{cog|zza|riz}}. Theorized to come to Iranian languages from {{cog|sa|व्रीहि}}.

Prior to Sanskrit, it is speculated to be possibly a borrowing from a {{der|en|dra}} language (compare {{cog|dra-pro|*wariñci||rice}}), or from {{der|en|aav}} languages further east.

Alternatively {{cog|gkm|ὄρυζα}} is said to be from {{cog|he|אורז|tr=órez}}, from South Arabian ''areez'' ultimately from {{cog|oty|𑀅𑀭𑀺𑀘𑀺}}.<ref>https://www.tamildigitallibrary.in/admin/assets/book/TVA_BOK_0013043_Proceedings_Of_The_Second_International_Conference_Seminar_Of_Tamil_Studies.pdf pg436</ref>

